 "lines": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "text": "Who has the biggest military on Earth? Let's start with the smallest.",
   "s": 0.0,
   "e": 4.24
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "text": "Costa Rica: zero. It abolished its army in 1948.",
   "s": 5.12,
   "e": 9.42
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "text": "Vatican City: 135 Swiss Guards. The smallest army in the world.",
   "s": 10.38,
   "e": 15.76
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "text": "Luxembourg: about 1,000 soldiers.",
   "s": 16.56,
   "e": 19.08
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "text": "Ireland: 7,500.",
   "s": 19.88,
   "e": 21.68
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "text": "The United Kingdom: around 140,000.",
   "s": 22.7,
   "e": 26.28
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "text": "Turkey: 355,000. The second biggest in NATO.",
   "s": 26.68,
   "e": 30.86
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "text": "Pakistan: 660,000.",
   "s": 32.1,
   "e": 34.54
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "text": "Russia: about 1.1 million.",
   "s": 35.16,
   "e": 36.98
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "text": "North Korea: 1.28 million, out of just 26 million people.",
   "s": 38.0,
   "e": 42.56
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "text": "The United States: 1.3 million.",
   "s": 43.22,
   "e": 45.68
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "text": "India: almost 1.5 million.",
   "s": 46.78,
   "e": 48.88
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "text": "And number one: China, with over 2 million active soldiers.",
   "s": 49.68,
   "e": 53.84
  },
  {
   "i": 13,
   "text": "But size isn't everything. America spends almost a trillion dollars a year on its military. More than the next nine countries combined.",
   "s": 54.52,
   "e": 63.08
  }
 ],
 "heard": "Who has the biggest military on Earth? Let's start with the smallest. Costa Rica zero. It abolished its army in 1948. Vatican City 135 Swiss Guards. The smallest army in the world. Luxembourg about 1 ,000 soldiers. Ireland 7 ,500. The United Kingdom around 140 ,000. Turkey 355 ,000. The second biggest in NATO. Pakistan 660 ,000. Russia about 1 .1 million. North Korea 1 .28 million, out of just 26 million people. The United States 1 .3 million. India almost 1 .5 million. And number one. China with over 2 million active soldiers. But size isn't everything. America spends almost a trillion dollars a year on its military. More than the next nine countries combined."
